he may not yet have been proven innocent  but brazil's former president louisiana  lula da silva  is no longer a felon and he's back on  the political scene  with an eye on next year's presidential  elections  i know that i was victim of the biggest  legal lie in the 500 years of history  i know my wife died due to the high  pressure and the stroke came faster  i was forbidden to even see my brother  inside a coffin  lula's speech on wednesday was the first  since a supreme court judge  overturned the corruption convictions  which put him behind bars  for 18 months and stripped him of his  political rights  banned from the 2018 elections the  leader of brazil's left-wing workers  party  is now seen as a political threat to  president  bolsonaro he says it's too soon to talk  about next year's presidential race  but he spoke like a candidate lula is  already a very popular leader  lulu presents himself as a moderate  leader  that this time and i think that the  first speech  that he gave this wednesday was an  attempt to show that himself  is a moderate it can  put together different groups different  sectors of the brazilian society and so  i think that he's a problem a real  problem for bolsonaro and for  bolsonaro's attempt  to be re-elected lula blasted bolsonaro  for  downplaying the kovit 19 pandemic which  has already claimed the lives  of almost 270 000 brazilians  the second largest death toll after the  united states  we have a president who says covet-19 is  a small flu  who says that only cowards fear the  virus and that he does not because he's  an athlete  this is not the way a president should  act in a civilized world  bolsonaro points out that lula is still  not off the legal hook  the decision to throw out the corruption  charges  was based on a technicality the supreme  court judge  said brazil's former president had been  tried by a court  in the southern city of kurichiba that  had no jurisdiction over his case  he may still be retried in the capital  brasilia  there are many legal twists and turns in  this case  the supreme court still has to decide  whether the judge who convicted lula  was impartial or had his own political  agenda  and colluded with the prosecution  meanwhile lula has started negotiating  an alliance with other left-wing parties  and even conservative politicians  who are not happy with president jair  bolsonaro  monica yanaki of al-jazeera rio de  janeiro
 

